{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-334069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4{x}^{2}y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=0.5,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current values $x$ and $y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ac140158747f1464abf6af2f63553af74a620f7d11ad2416483fa46e562b707"} {"question" "q-334069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4{x}^{2}y+4({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{x}^{2}y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{{{y}_{\\text{new}}-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-{x}^{2}y}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-{x}^{2}y.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ac140158747f1464abf6af2f63553af74a620f7d11ad2416483fa46e562b707"} {"question" "q-334069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65f50a505f9ce3456e7211a70d968570308a68bcc57004754eca2e822a539698"} {"question" "q-334069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ac140158747f1464abf6af2f63553af74a620f7d11ad2416483fa46e562b707"} {"question" "q-334069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-{x}^{2}y"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}y"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-{x}^{2}y"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-{x}^{2}y"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2{x}^{2}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ac140158747f1464abf6af2f63553af74a620f7d11ad2416483fa46e562b707"} {"question" "q-334069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-{x}^{2}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ac140158747f1464abf6af2f63553af74a620f7d11ad2416483fa46e562b707"} {"question" "q-334067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3{x}^{3}\\sqrt{y},\\,y(0)=4\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=0.5,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current values $x$ and $y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ac140158747f1464abf6af2f63553af74a620f7d11ad2416483fa46e562b707"} {"question" "q-334067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3{x}^{3}\\sqrt{y}+3({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{3}{4}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{3}{4}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{{{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{4}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{y}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{4}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{y}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ac140158747f1464abf6af2f63553af74a620f7d11ad2416483fa46e562b707"} {"question" "q-334067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65f50a505f9ce3456e7211a70d968570308a68bcc57004754eca2e822a539698"} {"question" "q-334067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ac140158747f1464abf6af2f63553af74a620f7d11ad2416483fa46e562b707"} {"question" "q-334067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{3}{4}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{y}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{y}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{4}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{3}{4}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}\\sqrt{y}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{4}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{y}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\t